Description: Harden TLS defaults to TLSv1.2+ and a restricted cipher list
 The daemon previously defaulted to TLSv1_plus (TLS 1.0 and later) and
 to the cipher string 'ALL:!MD5:@STRENGTH:@SECLEVEL=0', which also
 permits eNULL/LOW/EXP/RC4/MD5-grade ciphers. The code default is now
 TLSv1_2_plus and 'ALL:!eNULL:!LOW:!EXP:!RC4:!MD5:@STRENGTH:@SECLEVEL=0'
 ('ALL:!eNULL:!LOW:!EXP:!RC4:!MD5:@STRENGTH' on OpenSSL < 1.1.0, which
 has no @SECLEVEL).
 aNULL is intentionally retained: NRPE's default certificate-less mode
 negotiates anonymous-DH ciphers, so removing aNULL would leave the
 daemon with no usable ciphers out of the box. Deployments that
 configure ssl_cert_file can and should tighten this further with
 ssl_cipher_list (e.g. add !aNULL and @SECLEVEL=1).
 Note: this changes on-the-wire behaviour - peers using TLS < 1.2 or
 relying on eNULL/weak ciphers are now rejected. Older check_nrpe
 clients must be able to negotiate TLS 1.2; both sides can still be
 adjusted via ssl_version/ssl_cipher_list.
 The shipped sample configuration also sets ssl_version=TLSv1.2+
 explicitly so the floor is visible in nrpe.cfg.
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
---
--- a/src/nrpe.c	2026-10-02 22:54:59.604278211 +0200
+++ b/src/nrpe.c	2026-10-03 00:07:56.870514442 +0200
@@ -160,9 +160,9 @@
 
 SslParms sslprm = {
 #if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x10100000
-NULL, NULL, NULL, "ALL:!MD5:@STRENGTH:@SECLEVEL=0", TLSv1_plus, TRUE, 0, SSL_NoLogging
+NULL, NULL, NULL, "ALL:!eNULL:!LOW:!EXP:!RC4:!MD5:@STRENGTH:@SECLEVEL=0", TLSv1_2_plus, TRUE, 0, SSL_NoLogging
 #else
-NULL, NULL, NULL, "ALL:!MD5:@STRENGTH", TLSv1_plus, TRUE, 0, SSL_NoLogging
+NULL, NULL, NULL, "ALL:!eNULL:!LOW:!EXP:!RC4:!MD5:@STRENGTH", TLSv1_2_plus, TRUE, 0, SSL_NoLogging
 #endif
 };
 
--- a/sample-config/nrpe.cfg.in	2026-10-02 22:54:59.600558174 +0200
+++ b/sample-config/nrpe.cfg.in	2026-10-03 00:07:56.870674694 +0200
@@ -216,6 +216,9 @@
 
 #ssl_version=SSLv2+
 
+# this package is built with a TLSv1.2 minimum
+ssl_version=TLSv1.2+
+
 # SSL USE ADH
 # This is for backward compatibility and is DEPRECATED. Set to 1 to enable
 # ADH or 2 to require ADH. 1 is currently the default but will be changed
